# SignBridge — Hand Sign Recognition

SignBridge recognizes a small set of hand signs from a camera feed or a photo
and turns them into letters and words, with pages for live recognition,
learning the signs, a practice quiz, and progress tracking.

## How it works

- Hand landmarks are detected in the browser with MediaPipe Hand Landmarker.
- A rule-based classifier (`src/lib/signs.ts`) maps finger states to signs.
- Progress is stored locally in the browser (`src/lib/progress.ts`).

## Development

You need Node.js and npm — [install with nvm](https://github.com/nvm-sh/nvm#installing-and-updating).

```sh
npm i
npm run dev
```

